    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Caney Ridge sits on a ridge between two arms of Tenkiller Ferry Lake, known as Caney Creek and Dry Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caney_Ridge%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The area lies within the boundaries of the Cherokee Nation reservation in the hilly Cookson Hills region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/caney_ridge_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Oak-hickory forests dominate the landscape of Caney Ridge, providing a natural habitat for white-tailed deer and wild turkey.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
